From ab595073312630a52126b9e8832529ba654af03d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 17:48:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 081/638] [AROS] Define Base fallback contracts explicitly

AI_PHASE: Phase 3 - single-process headless shell
AI_STATUS: Chromium Base now supplies its required AROS path, allocation, watcher, process-iteration, and task-priority symbols.
ROOT_CAUSE: The first full link exposed platform implementations selected only for Linux, Fuchsia, or other kernels even where AROS needs a truthful native or unsupported contract.
FIX_REASON: Use DOS program identity and T: cache storage, libc unchecked allocation, fail-closed watcher/process enumeration, and current-task Exec priority mapping without procfs or inotify assumptions.
SCOPE: Base AROS source selection plus path and process adapters.
VALIDATION: All five affected objects and libbase.a build; symbol inspection confirms every previously unresolved Base entry in this group is defined.
RISK: File watching and process enumeration remain explicitly unavailable; priority changes apply only to the current Exec task.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
Continues: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
